      "question": "Following surgical resection of the corpus callosum (commissurotomy) to treat intractable epilepsy, split-brain patients were tested by Roger Sperry and Michael Gazzaniga using tachistoscopic visual presentation (flashing stimuli exclusively to the left or right visual hemifield). In \"Brain Bisection and the Unity of Consciousness\" (1971), what philosophical puzzle does Thomas Nagel deduce regarding the number of conscious minds in a split-brain patient?",
