      "question": "In \"The Symbol Grounding Problem\" (1990), Stevan Harnad analyzes how autonomous artificial agents can acquire genuine semantic meaning rather than mere formal syntactic manipulation. What is the classic analogy Harnad introduces to demonstrate why purely symbolic computational systems cannot ground their own symbols?",
