      "question": "In his landmark paper, \"Explanation in Artificial Intelligence: Insights from the Social Sciences\" (*Artificial Intelligence*, 2019), Tim Miller conducted a comprehensive cross-disciplinary survey of philosophy of science, cognitive psychology, and social linguistics to critique modern Explainable AI (XAI). What are the three foundational findings Miller establishes that computer scientists routinely overlook when designing automated explanation systems?",
