      "question": "In his landmark paper \"The Nature, Importance, and Difficulty of Machine Ethics\" (*IEEE Intelligent Systems*, 2006), philosopher James Moor developed a widely adopted four-part taxonomy to categorize the varying degrees to which an artificial machine can be considered an **ethical agent**. Which of the following accurately describes Moor's four classes of ethical agents?",
